      "note": "Fly from Mumbai to Kansai International Airport (KIX) in Osaka Bay. From KIX, board the Haruka limited express to Kyoto Station.\n\nCitations: [wv-04c7d000a4] Round trip for 2, rough estimate from ~6370 km distance."
    },
    "getting_around": "Take the Haruka limited express from Kansai International Airport (KIX) to Kyoto Station, or use the Nankai Railway Kyoto Access Ticket for a discounted ride to Tengachaya and onward to central Kyoto. Once in Kyoto, use the Kyoto Sightseeing Card for unlimited subway and bus travel, or hop on the Raku Bus routes 100/101 for quick tourist spots.\n\nCitations: [wv-04c7d000a4], [wv-408983d1ee], [wv-9fb915c77a], [wv-fae2418d83]",
    "visa": "Travelers from India should check the latest visa requirements for Japan on the official Japanese government immigration website. Generally, a short‑term tourist visa is required, but confirm the exact documents, processing time, and any changes due to COVID‑19 or other regulations.\n\nCitations: []",
    "currency_note": "The Japanese yen (JPY) is the local currency. Use a credit card with no foreign‑transaction fee or withdraw cash at ATMs in Kyoto. Exchange rates fluctuate, so check a reliable source before traveling.\n\nCitations: [] 1 JPY ≈ 0.006303 USD (ECB rate via Frankfurter)",
